<title>FINLAND: NOKIA WINS NOK 50 MLN GSM EXPANSION DEAL.</title>
<headline>NOKIA WINS NOK 50 MLN GSM EXPANSION DEAL.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish telecoms group Nokia Oy said in a statement on Tuesday it won an order worth 50 million Norwegian crowns to expand Norwegian telecoms operator Telenor Mobil's GSM network.</p>
<p>&quot;The expansion agreement is valued at approximately 50 million Norwegian crowns,&quot; Nokia said.  </p>
<p>Nokia said its ultra small PrimeSite base stations would allow Telenor Mobil to better focus coverage in target areas.</p>
<p>Nokia has delivered GSM (Global System for Mobile Communications) base station subsystems and equipment since 1994.</p>
<p>--Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 245, e-mail news@reuters.fi</p>
